BT /F2 14 Tf 54.00 572.00 Td (1. Introduction) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 545.00 Td (Aggregates are important materials used in construction, especially in concrete and asphalt. Their) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 532.00 Td (physical properties, such as particle size distribution and specific gravity, have a major effect on) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 519.00 Td (the strength, durability, and overall performance of construction materials. In this experiment,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 506.00 Td (sieve analysis and specific gravity tests were carried out to study these properties and assess the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 493.00 Td (suitability of the aggregate samples.) Tj ET
BT /F2 14 Tf 54.00 465.00 Td (2. Objectives) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 68.00 438.00 Td (- To determine the particle size distribution of the aggregate samples.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 68.00 425.00 Td (- To evaluate the gradation characteristics of fine and coarse aggregates.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 68.00 412.00 Td (- To calculate the specific gravity of the aggregate.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 68.00 399.00 Td (- To assess whether the aggregates are suitable for construction applications.) Tj ET
BT /F2 14 Tf 54.00 371.00 Td (3. Theory) Tj ET
BT /F2 11.5 Tf 54.00 338.00 Td (Sieve Analysis) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 314.00 Td (Sieve analysis is a testing method used to determine the distribution of particle sizes within an) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 301.00 Td (aggregate sample. The sample is passed through a series of standard sieves arranged from the largest) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 288.00 Td (opening size to the smallest. The mass retained on each sieve is measured and used to calculate the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 275.00 Td (percentage passing. These results help determine whether the aggregate is well graded or poorly) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 262.00 Td (graded.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 242.00 Td (The uniformity coefficient and coefficient of curvature are calculated using:) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 222.00 Td (Cu = D60 / D10) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 202.00 Td (Cc = \(D30\)^2 / \(D10 x D60\)) Tj ET
BT /F2 11.5 Tf 54.00 176.00 Td (Specific Gravity) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 152.00 Td (Specific gravity is the ratio of the density of an aggregate to the density of water. It is used to) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 139.00 Td (evaluate the relative density and quality of the material.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 119.00 Td (SG = W3 / [W3 - \(W1 - W2\)]) Tj ET
BT /F2 14 Tf 54.00 91.00 Td (4. Diagram of Apparatus) Tj ET
endstream
