BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 736.00 Td (Figure 1: Sieve Shaker Figure 2: Specific Gravity Frame) Tj ET
BT /F2 14 Tf 54.00 708.00 Td (5. Experimental Procedure) Tj ET
BT /F2 11.5 Tf 54.00 675.00 Td (Sieve Analysis Procedure) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 651.00 Td (The required maximum aggregate size was first used to select the appropriate sieves according to the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 638.00 Td (testing requirements. Before starting the test, all sieves were cleaned properly to avoid) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 625.00 Td (contamination from particles left from previous tests.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 605.00 Td (The sieves were arranged in descending order, with the largest sieve at the top and the smallest) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 592.00 Td (sieve above the collection pan. A representative aggregate sample was then weighed accurately using) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 579.00 Td (a digital balance.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 559.00 Td (The measured sample was placed into the top sieve, and the complete sieve stack was secured in the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 546.00 Td (mechanical sieve shaker. The shaker was operated continuously for approximately 10 minutes to) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 533.00 Td (separate the particles according to size.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 513.00 Td (After shaking was completed, the sieves were removed carefully, and the mass of aggregate retained) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 500.00 Td (on each sieve was recorded. Any particles stuck to the sieves were gently brushed off to ensure) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 487.00 Td (accurate weighing. The cumulative mass retained was then calculated, followed by the mass passing) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 474.00 Td (through each sieve. Finally, the percentage passing for each sieve size was determined using the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 461.00 Td (total sample mass.) Tj ET
BT /F2 11.5 Tf 54.00 435.00 Td (Specific Gravity Procedure) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 411.00 Td (The coarse aggregate sample was washed thoroughly to remove dust and fine particles that could) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 398.00 Td (affect the accuracy of the test. The cleaned aggregate was placed in a wire basket and fully) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 385.00 Td (immersed in water for 24 hours to allow it to become saturated.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 365.00 Td (The basket containing the aggregate was weighed while submerged in water, and this value was) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 352.00 Td (recorded as W1. The weight of the empty basket in water was then measured and recorded as W2.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 332.00 Td (After this, the aggregate was removed and dried with absorbent cloths until it reached a saturated) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 319.00 Td (surface dry condition. The surface-dry aggregate was weighed in air, and this value was recorded as) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 306.00 Td (W3. These measured values were then substituted into the specific gravity formula to calculate the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 293.00 Td (aggregate's specific gravity.) Tj ET
BT /F2 14 Tf 54.00 265.00 Td (6. Results) Tj ET
BT /F2 11.5 Tf 54.00 232.00 Td (Specific Gravity Data) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 208.00 Td (W1 = 2329 g W2 = 1082 g W3 = 2003 g) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 188.00 Td (Specific Gravity = 2.65) Tj ET
BT /F2 11.5 Tf 54.00 162.00 Td (Fine Aggregate) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 138.00 Td (Cu = 10.67 Cc = 1.50 Classification: Well graded) Tj ET
BT /F2 11.5 Tf 54.00 112.00 Td (Coarse Aggregate) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 88.00 Td (Cu = 1.88 Cc = 0.83 Classification: Poorly graded) Tj ET
endstream
