BT /F2 14 Tf 54.00 458.00 Td (8. Analysis and Discussion) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 431.00 Td (The calculated specific gravity of the aggregate is 2.65, which falls within the typical range for) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 418.00 Td (construction aggregates. This indicates that the material has a suitable density and can be) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 405.00 Td (considered appropriate for construction use.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 385.00 Td (The sieve analysis results show that the fine aggregate has a good range of particle sizes. Its) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 372.00 Td (uniformity coefficient is 10.67, and its coefficient of curvature is 1.50, which falls within the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 359.00 Td (acceptable range of 1 to 3. This means the fine aggregate is well graded. A well-graded aggregate) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 346.00 Td (helps improve compaction, reduce void spaces, and increase the strength and durability of) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 333.00 Td (construction materials.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 313.00 Td (In comparison, the coarse aggregate has a lower uniformity coefficient of 1.88 and a coefficient of) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 300.00 Td (curvature of 0.83. Since the coefficient of curvature is less than 1, the coarse aggregate is) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 287.00 Td (considered poorly graded. Poorly graded aggregates usually contain a limited range of particle) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 274.00 Td (sizes, which can lead to higher void content and reduced stability. Therefore, the coarse aggregate) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 261.00 Td (may need to be blended with other sizes to achieve better gradation.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 241.00 Td (Overall, the fine aggregate is more suitable for construction use based on its grading properties,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 228.00 Td (while the coarse aggregate may require modification before being used in structural applications.) Tj ET
BT /F2 14 Tf 54.00 200.00 Td (9. Conclusions) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 173.00 Td (The aggregate samples were tested to determine their particle size distribution and specific) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 160.00 Td (gravity. The specific gravity value of 2.65 indicates that the aggregate has a suitable density for) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 147.00 Td (construction purposes.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 127.00 Td (The fine aggregate was found to be well graded, making it suitable for use in construction materials) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 114.00 Td (where good compaction and strength are required. The coarse aggregate was classified as poorly) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 101.00 Td (graded because it had a limited particle size distribution. As a result, it may need to be combined) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 88.00 Td (with other aggregate sizes to improve its grading.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 68.00 Td (In conclusion, the experiment showed that specific gravity and gradation are important properties) Tj ET
endstream
